{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed and fix pushed as Gerrit 3263 (patch set 1, da19add4e79bb2a89f04aa8a964b3ea151e39745).\n\nReproduced in a sandbox store (temp git repo, rebar.init_repo, 1 unrelated commit, no remote): rebar.link(bug, target, caused_by) refused with exit 1 'has no commit referencing it'; rebar.transition(bug, in_progress, closed, close_class=regression, caused_by=target) succeeded and wrote caused_by -> target with provenance explicit.\n\nFix: transition_compute calls new refuse_unproven_caused_by right after resolve_explicit_caused_by, before any write. It reuses caused_by_refusal unchanged (no link/unlink code edited). Skipped when the close would write no explicit edge: blank flag, non-bug, self-target, already-active target.\n\nEvidence, fix-panther worktree, .venv/bin first on PATH:\n- tests/unit/test_caused_by_commitless_panther.py: on the pre-fix tree 1 of 7 failed (test_commitless_explicit_target_refuses_the_close: DID NOT RAISE); the 6 controls passed. All 7 pass after the fix.\n- The fix broke 3 existing tests that closed with an evidence-less explicit culprit (2 in test_caused_by_autoderive.py, 1 in facades/test_mcp.py) and would have broken the write-parity caused-by-bug-close row. They now give the culprit a referencing commit, as test_caused_by_relation.py already does for link. Added parity row caused-by-commitless-bug-close: REJECTED exit 1 on library, CLI, and MCP.\n- Targeted set (6 regression files from the plan plus partial_blame, link_endpoint_liveness, write_parity_oracle, facades/test_mcp, test_transition*): 214 passed.\n- make lint exit 0; make typecheck exit 0 (753 source files)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793703549969365001,"uuid":"2808c979-8141-4861-b55c-452a7eaaf7ac"}